---
/* "The small jobs a coach does." Five small jobs, each the top of a phone screen rebuilt from the shipped app:
   1 ios/TracendWidgets/RestLiveActivity.swift, ios/Shared/RestActivityAttributes.swift
   2 lib/features/train/widgets/exercise_detail_sheet.dart, train_parts.dart (next target and why)
   3 lib/features/readiness/pain_check_sheet.dart, safety_copy.dart, day_adjustment_card.dart
   4 lib/features/nutrition/widgets/nutrition_sheets.dart (candidate card, portion chooser, source badge)
   5 lib/features/coach/memory/coach_memory_screen.dart, widgets/fact_suggestion_chip.dart
   Every card is the same: a phone rising from the bottom of a stage, then a title and one line.
   The markup is each card's finished state; scripts/extras.js plays a one-shot on top. */
const island = '<span class="ex-island"></span>';
---
<section class="sec wrap" id="extras" aria-labelledby="extras-h">
  <div class="ex-head">
    <h2 class="sec-h disp" id="extras-h">The small jobs a coach does, done for you.</h2>
    <div class="ex-nav" data-ex-nav>
      <button type="button" class="ex-arrow" data-ex-prev aria-label="Previous" disabled><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M15 5l-7 7 7 7"/></svg></button>
      <button type="button" class="ex-arrow" data-ex-next aria-label="Next"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M9 5l7 7-7 7"/></svg></button>
    </div>
  </div>

  <ul class="ex-rail" role="list" tabindex="0" aria-label="Five things it handles between sessions" data-ex-rail>

    <li class="ex-card" data-ex="lock">
      <div class="ex-stage" aria-hidden="true">
        <div class="ex-scr app ex-ls"><Fragment set:html={island} />
          <p class="ex-ls-day">Monday</p>
          <p class="ex-ls-time a-num">18:52</p>
          <div class="ex-ls-card">
            <div class="ex-ls-layer ex-ls-set" data-ex-set>
              <div class="ex-ls-row">
                <div class="ex-ls-lab">
                  <span class="ex-ls-st"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24"><circle cx="12" cy="5" r="2"/><path d="M4 9h16M7 9v6M17 9v6M12 9v6M9 21l3-6 3 6"/></svg>Set 4 of 5</span>
                  <b class="ex-ls-ex">Back squat</b>
                </div>
                <span class="ex-ls-tgt a-num">120 kg &times; 5</span>
              </div>
              <div class="ex-ls-btns">
                <span class="ex-ls-btn lime" data-ex-log><svg viewBox="0 0 16 16"><path d="M3.2 8.4l3 3 6.6-6.8"/></svg>Log set<i class="ex-ripple"></i></span>
                <span class="ex-ls-btn raised">Open</span>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="ex-ls-layer ex-ls-rest" data-ex-rest>
              <div class="ex-ls-row">
                <div class="ex-ls-lab">
                  <span class="ex-ls-st"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24"><circle cx="12" cy="13" r="7.5"/><path d="M12 9v4l2.5 1.5M9.5 2.5h5"/></svg>Rest</span>
                  <b class="ex-ls-ex">Back squat</b>
                  <span class="ex-ls-dt">Next: Set 4 of Back squat</span>
                </div>
                <span class="ex-ls-cd a-num" data-ex-cd>0:00</span>
              </div>
              <div class="ex-ls-btns">
                <span class="ex-ls-btn raised">+30s</span>
                <span class="ex-ls-btn raised"><svg viewBox="0 0 16 16"><path d="M3 3.5l6 4.5-6 4.5zM12.5 3v10"/></svg>Skip</span>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p class="sr-only">Example Lock Screen. A card shows set 4 of 5, Back squat, 120 kilograms for 5, with a lime Log set button and an Open button. During rest it shows a countdown with plus 30 seconds and Skip.</p>
      <h3 class="ex-h">Log sets from your Lock Screen.</h3>
      <p class="ex-p">Your next set and rest timer wait there. One tap logs it.</p>
    </li>

    <li class="ex-card" data-ex="prog">
      <div class="ex-stage" aria-hidden="true">
        <div class="ex-scr app ex-pg"><Fragment set:html={island} />
          <p class="ex-pg-h"><b>Back squat</b><span>Next session</span></p>
          <div class="ex-tiles">
            <div class="ex-tile ex-tile-next" data-ex-tile><span class="k">Next target</span><span class="v a-num"><span class="ex-roll"><span class="o">120</span><span class="n">122.5</span></span> kg &times; 5</span></div>
            <div class="ex-tile"><span class="k">Sets</span><span class="v a-num">5 &times; 5</span></div>
          </div>
          <p class="ex-pg-why" data-ex-why>Every set reached the top of the range last time. Add weight and start the reps again.</p>
          <div class="ex-list">
            <p><span>Last time</span><b class="a-num">120 kg &times; 5, 5, 5, 5, 5</b></p>
            <p><span>Your best</span><b class="a-num">120 kg &times; 5</b></p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p class="sr-only">Example exercise screen for the back squat. Last time: 120 kilograms for 5 on all five sets. Every set reached the top of the range, so the next target is 122.5 kilograms for 5.</p>
      <h3 class="ex-h">It tells you when to add weight.</h3>
      <p class="ex-p">Hit the top reps on every set and the target goes up. Fall short and it holds.</p>
    </li>

    <li class="ex-card" data-ex="pain">
      <div class="ex-stage" aria-hidden="true">
        <div class="ex-scr app ex-pn"><Fragment set:html={island} />
          <p class="ex-scr-t">Pain or discomfort</p>
          <p class="ex-pn-q">Where?</p>
          <div class="ex-pn-chips"><span class="on">Knee</span><span>Lower back</span><span>Shoulder</span></div>
          <p class="ex-pn-q">How strong right now?</p>
          <div class="ex-pn-sev"><span>1</span><span>2</span><span>3</span><span>4</span><span class="on">5</span><span>6</span><span>7</span><span>8</span><span>9</span><span>10</span></div>
          <div class="ex-pn-card" data-ex-res>
            <b class="ex-pn-t">Easier on your joints today</b>
            <p class="ex-pn-l"><span class="ex-pn-old">Back squat</span><svg viewBox="0 0 16 16"><path d="M2.5 8h10M9 4l4 4-4 4"/></svg><span class="ex-pn-new">Goblet squat</span></p>
            <p class="ex-pn-s">Only today changes.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p class="sr-only">Example pain check. Where: knee. How strong right now: 5 out of 10. The result reads Easier on your joints today: back squat is swapped for goblet squat, and only today changes.</p>
      <h3 class="ex-h">Sore knee? It works around it.</h3>
      <p class="ex-p">It swaps or shortens the exercise, and tells you when to see a professional.</p>
    </li>

    <li class="ex-card" data-ex="label">
      <div class="ex-stage" aria-hidden="true">
        <div class="ex-scr app ex-lb"><Fragment set:html={island} />
          <div class="ex-lb-photo" data-ex-photo>
            <span class="ex-lb-t">Nutrition Facts</span>
            <span class="ex-lb-sv">Serving size 1 bar (60 g)</span>
            <span class="ex-lb-r big"><b>Calories</b><b>210</b></span>
            <span class="ex-lb-r"><span>Protein</span><span>20 g</span></span>
            <span class="ex-lb-r"><span>Carbohydrate</span><span>22 g</span></span>
            <span class="ex-lb-r"><span>Fat</span><span>7 g</span></span>
            <b class="ex-scan" data-ex-scan></b>
          </div>
          <div class="ex-cand" data-ex-cand>
            <div class="ex-cand-row">
              <span class="ex-cb"><svg viewBox="0 0 16 16"><path d="M3.2 8.4l3 3 6.6-6.8"/></svg></span>
              <span class="ex-cand-t"><b>Protein bar</b><span class="a-num">60 g &middot; 210 kcal &middot; 20 g protein</span></span>
              <span class="ex-badge" data-ex-badge>From label</span>
            </div>
            <div class="ex-seg"><span class="on">1 serving</span><span>Whole pack</span><span>Grams</span></div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p class="sr-only">Example meal review. A photo of a nutrition label becomes one food: Protein bar, 60 grams, 210 calories, 20 grams of protein, marked From label. A portion chooser offers 1 serving, Whole pack or Grams.</p>
      <h3 class="ex-h">Snap the label, not just the plate.</h3>
      <p class="ex-p">It reads the label and checks the math. You pick the portion.</p>
    </li>

    <li class="ex-card" data-ex="mem">
      <div class="ex-stage" aria-hidden="true">
        <div class="ex-scr app ex-mm"><Fragment set:html={island} />
          <p class="ex-scr-t">What Coach remembers</p>
          <ul class="ex-facts">
            <li class="due" data-ex-fact><svg class="ex-ic" viewBox="0 0 16 16"><circle cx="8" cy="8" r="6.2"/><path d="M8 4.6V8l2.2 1.4"/></svg><span>Knee pain on deep squats</span></li>
            <li data-ex-fact><svg class="ex-ic" viewBox="0 0 16 16"><path d="M8 1.6l5.2 2v3.7c0 3.2-2.1 5.6-5.2 7.1-3.1-1.5-5.2-3.9-5.2-7.1V3.6z"/><path d="M5.6 8l1.7 1.7 3.2-3.4"/></svg><span>Trains before work</span></li>
            <li data-ex-fact><svg class="ex-ic" viewBox="0 0 16 16"><path d="M8 1.6l5.2 2v3.7c0 3.2-2.1 5.6-5.2 7.1-3.1-1.5-5.2-3.9-5.2-7.1V3.6z"/><path d="M5.6 8l1.7 1.7 3.2-3.4"/></svg><span>Vegetarian</span></li>
          </ul>
          <div class="ex-ask-card" data-ex-ask>
            <p class="ex-ask-h">Knee pain on deep squats</p>
            <p class="ex-ask-r">Coach would like to check that this still applies.</p>
            <div class="ex-ask-b"><span>Edit</span><span class="lime">Still true</span></div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p class="sr-only">Example Coach memory. Saved facts: Knee pain on deep squats, Trains before work, Vegetarian. The knee fact is due for a check: Coach would like to check that this still applies, with Edit and Still true.</p>
      <h3 class="ex-h">It remembers what you tell it.</h3>
      <p class="ex-p">Your limits shape every plan. Later it asks: still true?</p>
    </li>

  </ul>
  <div class="ex-foot">
    <div class="ex-dots" aria-hidden="true" data-ex-dots><i class="on"></i><i></i><i></i><i></i><i></i></div>
    <span class="ex-tag">Example screens</span>
  </div>
</section>
